   859	/**Function*************************************************************
   860	
   861	  Synopsis    [Returns 1 if an stmap area-sensitive mode should reject a cut.]
   862	
   863	  Description [The area-sensitive guards are evaluated after matching the
   864	  candidate cut because their hypotheses need the candidate's actual mapper
   865	  area. In stmap6 exact-area recovery, a wide high-fanout cut is rejected only
   866	  when the existing match has slack and the candidate does not save at least
   867	  half an inverter area. In stmap7, the area-saving override additionally
   868	  requires more than two inverter delays of slack and excludes the highest
   869	  fanout-risk bucket. In stmap8, the override is further rejected when the
   870	  candidate match worsens mapper arrival by more than one quarter of an
   871	  inverter delay. In stmap9, middle-slack candidates can recover area only
   872	  when they are outside the highest fanout bucket, do not worsen mapper
   873	  arrival, and save at least one inverter area. In stmap10, that middle-slack
   874	  relief also requires the mapper node to be no deeper than level 96. In
   875	  stmap11, that depth window is tightened to level 64. In stmap12, the same
   876	  tight-depth relief is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. In
   877	  stmap13, the same decision path also records exact-area guard statistics. In
   878	  stmap14, the lower-moderate middle-slack relief must save two inverter areas
   879	  instead of one. In stmap15, one-inverter relief is restored only after the
   880	  mapper observes a high lower-moderate/middle-slack profile. In stmap16, the
   881	  same behavior also reports each admitted relief choice. In stmap17, the
   882	  adaptive one-inverter relief threshold also requires a material mapper-arrival
   883	  improvement; arrival-neutral choices keep the stricter two-inverter fallback.
   884	  In stmap18, the same decisions are preserved while near-miss rejected
   885	  middle-slack candidates are logged. In stmap19, pre-profile one-inverter
   886	  relief is seeded only by candidates with the same material arrival gain. In
   887	  stmap20, the pre-profile seed is further limited to shallow nodes. In
   888	  stmap21, deeper pre-profile seeds are allowed only with a much larger mapper
   889	  arrival gain. In stmap22, the same deep-seed path is relaxed to a moderate
   890	  mapper-arrival gain. In stmap23, moderate deep seeds also need near-critical
   891	  existing mapper slack. In stmap24, the moderate deep slack gate is tightened
   892	  to the lower edge of the critical slack window. In stmap25, the stmap24 rule
   893	  is kept, and one moderate deep seed from the next slack band is admitted for
   894	  ablation. In stmap26, the first such moderate seed is skipped and only the
   895	  second qualifying seed is admitted. In stmap27, moderate deep candidates in
   896	  the next slack band are admitted unless they match the high-reference,
   897	  low-slack, stronger-moderate signature isolated by stmap26. In stmap28, that
   898	  hard blocker is replaced by a soft area-margin penalty on high-reference
   899	  moderate seeds whose slack and arrival-gain ratios resemble load-risky
   900	  choices. In stmap29, the high-reference penalty is made continuous over the
   901	  same seed band. In stmap30, the same load-risk surface is extended to
   902	  high-reference strong deep seeds with a smaller continuous penalty. In
   903	  stmap31, the strong-seed gain slope is damped to probe the penalty threshold.]
   904	
   905	  SideEffects []
   906	
   907	  SeeAlso     []
   908	
   909	***********************************************************************/
   910	static int Map_MatchSkipAreaSensitiveFanout( Map_Man_t * p, Map_Node_t * pNode, Map_Cut_t * pCut, int fPhase, Map_Match_t * pMatchBest, Map_Match_t * pMatch )
